desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Global Access Modifiers",
	title_zh: "检测到Global Access Modifiers",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-global-access-modifiers",
	risk: "Best-Practice",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `global-access-modifiers` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/apex/lang/best-practice/ncino/accessModifiers/GlobalAccessModifiers.yaml).
Original message: Global classes, methods, and variables should be avoided (especially in managed packages) as they can never be deleted or changed in signature. Always check twice if something needs to be global.

CWE: CWE-284: Improper Access Control
References:
- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/284.html
Note: original paths.exclude ['*Test*', '*test*'] not applied (SF path filter limitation).
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Follow the framework's secure configuration guidance; remove or replace the flagged pattern.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.cls": <<<POS
global wyVuHK9XQoiyEygHCclVZf

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*.cls}.pattern_regex_not(/global [A-Za-z0-9_]{3,}/, /\/\/(\s+([a-zA-Z]+\s+)+)[a-zA-Z]+/, /[*](\s+([a-zA-Z]+\s+)+)[a-zA-Z]+/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Global Access Modifiers",
	title_zh: "检测到Global Access Modifiers",
	message: "Global Access Modifiers",
}
